Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.94,0:00:15.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's finished.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.90,0:00:16.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:19.07,0:00:22.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's okay.\NThis is perfect.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.04,0:00:30.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Let's do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.44,0:00:51.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.44,0:00:58.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is the scientific technique of understanding the structure of matter,\Ndecomposing it, and then reconstructing it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.69,0:01:05.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If performed skillfully, it is even \Npossible to create gold out of lead.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.45,0:01:12.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, as it is a science, there are some natural principles in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.04,0:01:20.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Only one thing can be created from something else of a certain mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.80,0:01:23.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the Principle of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.85,0:01:30.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What? What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:30.35,0:01:31.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on, Winry!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.93,0:01:35.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Principle of Equivalent Exchange \Nstates that in order to obtain something,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.90,0:01:39.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,something else of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.65,0:01:43.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an1}Is that some kind of maxim?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:43.49,0:01:48.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an1}Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout sacrificing something?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.79,0:01:50.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an1}Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:51.37,0:01:54.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!\NAlphonse!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.79,0:01:58.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit! I'm not about to let this happen!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.13,0:02:01.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This wasn't... This wasn't supposed to...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.80,0:02:04.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dammit!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.30,0:02:07.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's been taken away!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.64,0:02:16.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mom?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.98,0:02:55.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm starving...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.81,0:03:03.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If only there were some grass growing here,\NI could change it into bread.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.57,0:03:05.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.07,0:03:07.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.82,0:03:10.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al? Al?!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.20,0:03:12.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right here!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.54,0:03:16.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Help me, Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.21,0:03:20.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You got buried again?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.55,0:03:25.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do that one more time,\Nand I'm leaving you behind!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.46,0:03:26.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.38,0:03:29.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't "but" me!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.30,0:03:32.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:35.73,0:03:37.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Wait up, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.48,0:03:39.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm not waiting!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.48,0:03:41.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Stop!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.98,0:03:41.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm not stopping!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.56,0:03:43.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Straighten up!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.27,0:03:45.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I won't get buried again!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.30,0:04:05.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, are you okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.92,0:04:08.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all your fault for not stopping.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.59,0:04:13.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't think anyone would stop \Nif they were told to do so like you did.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.93,0:04:16.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, so that's it?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.18,0:04:20.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so thirsty...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.69,0:04:24.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.28,0:04:26.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.22,0:04:27.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.28,0:04:29.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water! Water! Water! Water!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:29.45,0:04:30.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water! Water! Water!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:36.49,0:04:39.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}This{\i0} is what I've been smelling all along?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.37,0:04:41.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.04,0:04:44.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Blood?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.96,0:04:47.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,More like blood-red wine.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.51,0:04:48.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.97,0:04:50.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is off-limits to kids, you know!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.34,0:04:53.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sorry, I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.97,0:04:57.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As travelers, you wouldn't have known that there was wine coming out of there, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.26,0:04:59.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Wow! Look at that suit of armor!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.11,0:05:01.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The town of Liore here must be pretty prosperous, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.10,0:05:02.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Having a wine fountain and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.60,0:05:04.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, you might say that.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.40,0:05:06.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, whoops, gotta do this...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:32.84,0:05:35.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of God's children,\Nwho live upon this land,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.22,0:05:39.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,pray in faith, that ye may be saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.14,0:05:43.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Sun God Leto\Nilluminates thy footsteps.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.15,0:05:45.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the deal?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.15,0:05:47.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}God, who watches over thee, \Nhas descended from his throne,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.48,0:05:47.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A religious broadcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.94,0:05:51.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As far as I'm concerned, I should be the one \Nasking "What's the deal?" of you guys.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.94,0:05:51.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}and saves thee from all thy sins.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.32,0:05:56.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I am Leto's representative, and thy father.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.96,0:05:59.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you guys street performers or something?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.96,0:05:59.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I offer up this prayer.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.41,0:06:03.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now look here, Pop!\NWhere'd you get that idea from?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.41,0:06:06.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you're not performers, then what have you come all this way for?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.67,0:06:09.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, there's something we're looking for.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.59,0:06:11.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So, what's the story with this broadcast?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.96,0:06:13.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's Cornello-sama.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.22,0:06:14.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and like, who is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.26,0:06:17.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't know the representative of the Sun God Leto?!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.35,0:06:19.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No, so who is he?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.60,0:06:23.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's Cornello-sama, \Na performer of miraculous works!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.23,0:06:27.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's because of him that this forsaken town in the middle of the desert
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.23,0:06:28.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,has become as prosperous as it is!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.19,0:06:31.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He really is an incredible man!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.19,0:06:34.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.28,0:06:37.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The works that man does are truly miraculous!\NI'm not all that interested in religion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.03,0:06:40.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shall we get going, Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:40.33,0:06:41.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Y-Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.00,0:06:49.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now you've done it, sir!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.71,0:06:51.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what happens when you\Ngo around wearing such an outfit!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:52.00,0:06:54.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sorry, sorry! I'll fix it right away.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.92,0:06:55.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fix it?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.97,0:06:57.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm so sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.64,0:07:00.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, I'll do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.39,0:07:00.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:03.31,0:07:04.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.81,0:07:05.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a transmutation circle.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.35,0:07:07.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.81,0:07:12.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Okay, here goes!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.61,0:07:27.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}As the representative of Leto, \NI pour out my love unto thee always.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.58,0:07:27.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a surprise! You guys can also perform miraculous acts?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.50,0:07:28.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you mean by that?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.08,0:07:31.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're alchemists.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.09,0:07:35.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're the Elric brothers.\NOur reputation is fairly widespread.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.05,0:07:37.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.55,0:07:40.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it wasn't a miracle?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.18,0:07:43.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've never heard of any alchemists around these parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.43,0:07:47.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's the Fullmetal Alchemist, Edward Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.89,0:07:51.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're famous around East City.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.48,0:07:54.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Said to be an alchemist prodigy.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:57.70,0:07:59.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.41,0:08:00.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So that's it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.36,0:08:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is why your\Nnickname is "Fullmetal"!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.53,0:08:04.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you really that famous? Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.58,0:08:07.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, not me...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.91,0:08:08.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:09.29,0:08:10.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean the little guy there?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.58,0:08:14.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who are you calling a bean sprout, too tiny to even notice?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.67,0:08:16.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nobody called you that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.88,0:08:20.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Things sure are bustling today!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.68,0:08:24.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.60,0:08:28.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, I haven't seen these folks around.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.52,0:08:33.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm Alphonse Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.52,0:08:37.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And I'm the Fullmetal Alchemist, his older brother, Edward Elric.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.61,0:08:40.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh my, {\i1}you're{\i0} the older brother?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.86,0:08:42.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now, now...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.78,0:08:46.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, are you already done shopping for your offering?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.04,0:08:48.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.16,0:08:52.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, take these two along with you to the Church of Leto.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:52.37,0:08:56.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They say they're looking for something, so they could ask for God's grace.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.88,0:08:58.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, but we don't...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.88,0:09:00.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's all right.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.34,0:09:03.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There are\Npilgrim's quarters there too.\NPlease, make your stay there.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.14,0:09:05.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:05.10,0:09:06.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.64,0:09:09.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In that case, let's take them up on it, okay, Al?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:09.85,0:09:12.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,O-Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.69,0:09:19.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose sure has gotten\Na lot more cheerful, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:19.44,0:09:22.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah. That's thanks to the Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.70,0:09:25.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Especially after what happened.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.37,0:09:34.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.79,0:09:38.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That woman at the shop earlier...\NHave we ever seen her before?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.00,0:09:40.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.76,0:09:42.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It'll be okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.05,0:09:45.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm sure you'll soon find what you're looking for.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.72,0:09:47.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And what's more...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:48.39,0:09:51.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you pray, I'm sure you'll grow taller!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.64,0:09:54.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What did you say?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.55,0:09:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Don't go making fun of me!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.55,0:09:56.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}I'm sorry!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.98,0:09:59.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.98,0:09:59.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Hey, wait up!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.36,0:10:04.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Pray in faith, that thy entreaties may be accorded thee.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:05.45,0:10:11.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,May all of his children\Nreceive the grace of his light,\Nboth today and tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.83,0:10:16.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Nicely done, Minister.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.13,0:10:19.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you so much for your favorable words today.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.55,0:10:21.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Minister...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.21,0:10:23.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, Rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.84,0:10:28.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, may I put some travelers up\Nin the pilgrim's quarters?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.06,0:10:32.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You seem to do all you can each day for God, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.14,0:10:36.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I serve the Lord Leto always.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.90,0:10:38.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's why...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.90,0:10:44.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,God sees your good works.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.28,0:10:48.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The reason your miracle has not occurred is that the time is still a little too short.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.49,0:10:51.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.25,0:10:58.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? You say that's the grave of Rose-san's beloved?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.25,0:11:02.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Without anyone to rely on, and having lost her boyfriend in an accident,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.59,0:11:05.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose-san clings to\NMinister Cornello's teachings.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.38,0:11:09.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,When all the while, there's no way the dead can come back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.64,0:11:11.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They {\i1}do{\i0} appear to come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.77,0:11:15.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As the living are given an immortal soul,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:15.73,0:11:17.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so are the dead given resurrection.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.06,0:11:21.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The testament is in the\Nmiraculous works, they say.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:23.32,0:11:25.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sounds fishy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.88,0:11:46.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.17,0:11:49.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no two ways about it.\NThat metamorphic reaction must be alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.14,0:11:52.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sure is. But still, the laws—
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.60,0:11:54.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh, it's you two!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.31,0:11:57.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you think about\NCornello-sama's miraculous works?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.60,0:12:00.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how you slice it,\Nthat's alchemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.15,0:12:02.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This Cornello guy is just a swindling bastard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.32,0:12:05.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's not entirely established.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:05.61,0:12:07.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We just know that he's ignoring the laws.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.78,0:12:08.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The laws?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.20,0:12:14.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemy isn't the creation of something out of nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.33,0:12:18.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a scientific technique,\Nwhich obeys the laws of nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.50,0:12:23.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can only get something out of another thing of the same mass.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.67,0:12:27.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like how I could only make a radio that was the same size as before.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.01,0:12:32.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't make it a bigger radio,\Nor change it into a piece of paper, or a tree, or something.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.68,0:12:37.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's how, if you want to obtain something, you need something of equal value.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.35,0:12:39.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But the old guy up there is disregarding that.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.85,0:12:41.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's like I've been saying,\Nthey're miracles!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.07,0:12:55.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can you bring about\Nsuch a miracle using alchemy?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.29,0:12:59.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And Cain will soon be...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.42,0:13:02.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Elric brothers?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:03.04,0:13:08.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I heard that the older brother received the\Ntitle of State Alchemist when he was twelve.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.05,0:13:10.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's called the Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.13,0:13:13.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That little brat?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.14,0:13:14.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's a dog of the military.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:15.64,0:13:19.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The military has cast their gaze upon our bountiful town here, and plans to intervene.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.10,0:13:23.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The people—my children—must be saved.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.35,0:13:25.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Cray...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:26.48,0:13:28.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I shall carry out the will of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.94,0:13:32.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am grateful to you for\Nbringing this to my attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.49,0:13:36.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just having that boy here is troubling, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.41,0:13:39.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is still one other way,\Njust in case.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.80,0:13:52.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just by serving God so dutifully,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.05,0:13:55.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,someone who is dead will\Ncome back to life at some point?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.76,0:13:58.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, absolutely.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.94,0:14:11.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Water, 35 liters; carbon, 20 kilograms; ammonia, 4 liters; lime, 1.5 kilograms;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:12.11,0:14:18.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,phosphorus, 800 grams; salt, 250 grams; saltpeter, 100 grams; sulfur, 80 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.66,0:14:22.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,fluorine, 7.5 grams;\Niron, 5 grams; silicon, 3 grams;
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.70,0:14:24.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and a small amount of\Nfifteen other elements.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:24.96,0:14:25.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's that?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:26.17,0:14:32.09,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is the material makeup of a single average adult human body if you were to calculate it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.26,0:14:35.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Despite being able to know\Nthis much through science,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:35.47,0:14:39.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there's never been a successful reported case of anyone actually transmuting a human body.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:40.01,0:14:45.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For several centuries, scientists have been researching what it is that's missing.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.27,0:14:49.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Their efforts are more worthwhile than just praying and waiting around, wouldn't you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.40,0:14:52.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,By the way, all of these ingredients
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.44,0:14:55.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,can be bought at a market with the spare change any child might have.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.24,0:14:58.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Humans can be made for cheap, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.57,0:15:01.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,People aren't things!\NWould you blaspheme God?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.04,0:15:05.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Alchemists are scientists,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:05.37,0:15:08.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so God is something ambiguous, which we don't believe in.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.54,0:15:14.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's ironic, since we're the ones who are closest to being gods.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.55,0:15:16.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You are not a god!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.30,0:15:20.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Neither is the sun.\NIt's just a very hot mass of stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.22,0:15:24.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you get too close to the sun,\Nall you do is burn up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.10,0:15:33.40,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez, Brother, you're just getting Rose-san upset at you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.61,0:15:37.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry. Your brother\Nwill be coming with you soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.20,0:15:45.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Disciple Cray!\NWhat are you doing?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.91,0:15:47.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They are enemies of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.42,0:15:50.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All of this is God's will!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.08,0:15:51.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, you startled me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.76,0:16:00.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My head!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.64,0:16:02.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Stee-rike!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.76,0:16:05.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's going on here?! His head...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.60,0:16:06.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.10,0:16:08.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is how I am.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:11.15,0:16:12.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's nothing inside him!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.27,0:16:19.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You could call this the punishment I got\Nfor setting foot on holy ground,\Nwhich as a person, I should never\Nhave encroached upon.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.57,0:16:20.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Both me...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:21.11,0:16:22.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.16,0:16:29.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.08,0:16:33.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's true!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:33.59,0:16:37.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's just like the Minister said!\N{\i1}Those two are enemies of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.47,0:16:43.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No one ever told us\Nabout this place.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.14,0:16:46.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.31,0:16:51.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How good of you to\Nbring them here, Rose.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.07,0:17:00.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A State Alchemist, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.32,0:17:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had a feeling you would come here sooner or later.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.99,0:17:05.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that because you're a swindler who deceives his believers?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.37,0:17:06.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or instead...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:06.45,0:17:08.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it because you possess the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.79,0:17:11.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.25,0:17:19.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Transmuting without drawing any transmutation circles\Nwhile disregarding the\NLaw of Equivalent Exchange...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.42,0:17:21.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There could be only one answer.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.09,0:17:22.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Quite so.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.47,0:17:27.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The enchanted sorcery amplifier, said to exist only in legend—
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.85,0:17:29.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the Philosopher's Stone!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.56,0:17:31.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I've been looking for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.60,0:17:36.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll get right to the point.\NHand over the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.65,0:17:39.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do that, and I won't say a thing to the people in town.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.15,0:17:43.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean to deprive me of this?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.16,0:17:47.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If my miraculous works cease,\Nwhat would become of this town?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:48.70,0:17:50.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right, Rose?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.54,0:17:53.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose! That guy is just\Na third-rate con man!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.67,0:17:58.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I returned life to this town, just as it was about to crumble from internal strife.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.34,0:18:01.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I created water and turned it into wine,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.34,0:18:04.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,built buildings, and even\Ngave money to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.93,0:18:08.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am the representative of God!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:08.39,0:18:13.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Do you intend to deprive the\Npeople of this city of their God?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.27,0:18:15.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is that how absolute the\Norders of the military are?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:16.23,0:18:20.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't care less \Nabout military orders.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.27,0:18:20.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:20.32,0:18:21.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I need...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.32,0:18:23.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We need that thing!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.24,0:18:26.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.41,0:18:30.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why, even knowing it will rob us of hope, are you still after it?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.45,0:18:32.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, we're going to—
Dialogue: 0,0:18:31.58,0:18:32.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no use.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.83,0:18:41.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, why don't we have a look at the power of the Philosopher's Stone?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.43,0:18:49.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.47,0:18:51.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Your armor has turned against you, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.22,0:18:54.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't very well draw a transmutation circle in that sand, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.99,0:19:14.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Using the Philosopher's Stone,\Nyou synthesized a kindred life form?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.96,0:19:17.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, a Chimera!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.42,0:19:24.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It looks like...\Ntaking him on barehanded...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.22,0:19:28.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is going to be...\Ntough!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.48,0:19:38.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What?! You transmuted without using a transmutation circle?!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.28,0:19:47.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Go get him!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.34,0:20:10.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How do you like that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:12.93,0:20:14.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just kidding.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.98,0:20:20.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not getting away!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.66,0:20:42.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What's the matter,\Nyou pussy bastard?\NGet yourself a good taste.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.55,0:20:53.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Gluttony, that boy...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:57.02,0:20:58.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I-Impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.14,0:21:01.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,How could his claws not tear through your leg?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.35,0:21:05.32,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Or his fangs crush your arm?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.73,0:21:08.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't tell me you're...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.32,0:21:10.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah, that's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:11.40,0:21:13.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Rose, take a good look.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.49,0:21:16.70,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is the body of one who performs a human transmutation...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.12,0:21:20.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,of one who encroaches upon God or whoever's territory.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.00,0:21:23.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is what happens to such transgressors!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:25.63,0:21:29.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A mechanical... arm and leg? Automail?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.51,0:21:32.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You performed human transmutation?!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.76,0:21:36.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've committed that\Nwhich is most sanctioned!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.35,0:21:39.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've had your bodies\Ntaken over to the other side!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.23,0:21:44.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}If you get too close to the sun,\Nall you do is burn up.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.11,0:21:48.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,So this is why your title is "Fullmetal"!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:50.15,0:21:52.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The Fullmetal Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.18,0:23:40.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.97,0:23:42.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 2: "Body of the Sanctioned"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.89,0:23:45.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A false Philosopher's Stone—
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.56,0:23:49.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,it is sure to bring with it\Nfalse peace and false promises.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.90,0:23:52.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, the tears it brings are not false.
